    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0833" n="821" xml:id="pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 European War 1939/7347: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-17T20:00:00-04:00">September 17, 1943—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 18—3:02 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1643. Reference my 1631, September 15, 7 p.m.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d786-f1"/>
                    The Embassy believes that the visit of Fernández to Washington affords a good
                    opportunity to take up the question of going forward with a program of expulsion
                    from Chile and internment in the United States of the dangerous Axis nationals
                    here in order to implement Chile’s rupture of relations with the Axis. As the
                    Department is aware, no Axis nationals have been interned and the measures taken
                    against the dangerous Axis nationals in Chile have been most ineffective.</p>
                <p>Please bring this telegram to the Ambassador’s attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
